+	The mapping is shared with the OS page cache: the pages cost
+	almost no private memory and remain evictable by the kernel.
+	The buffer is immutable, like a shared-data buffer; the mapping
+	is released when the buffer is dropped.
+
+	Only for files that are not truncated while mapped (reading a
+	page past a shrunken end raises SIGBUS), such as system fonts.
+
+	Returns NULL if mapping is not supported on this platform or if
+	the file cannot be mapped; callers are expected to fall back to
+	fz_read_file.
+*/
